From: MedPlatform <noreply@medplatform.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] linux-explicit-synchronization-v1: enough of it for a vendor EGL's clients

With the display bound, a client of the vendor's EGL draws - and logs
"__buffer_handle_release: ERROR: invalid state=1" at every frame. Under a
compositor that offers zwp_linux_explicit_synchronization_v1 the same
client hands over a fence with each frame, cycles four buffers and takes
them back through zwp_linux_buffer_release_v1; wl_buffer.release is never
sent to it. Without the protocol it falls back to two buffers, takes the
older one back by itself, and objects to the release when it reads it.

The protocol half is Simon Ser's unmerged implementation (4f5909ca6,
785549bc3). What that one did with render timelines, which 0.17 does not
have, is done here in the plainest way that is correct:

- the acquire fence is waited for at commit, bounded at 100 ms, before
  anything can sample the buffer. A frame not ready by then is shown as it
  is and the log says so once;
- the release is "immediate_release", sent when wl_buffer.release would
  have been and instead of it. A buffer type asks
  linux_explicit_synchronization_v1_release_buffer() first; the EGL client
  buffers and linux-dmabuf buffers do.

Advertised only when the display was bound to EGL, so nothing changes for
a compositor on a driver that never asked for that.
WLR_NO_EXPLICIT_SYNC=1 leaves the global out.

Not done: a release fence of the compositor's own. The old buffer is no
longer sampled once the new one is committed, but a frame already handed
to the GPU may still be reading it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [upstream chose linux-drm-syncobj-v1 instead]
---
diff --git a/include/types/wlr_linux_explicit_synchronization_v1.h b/include/types/wlr_linux_explicit_synchronization_v1.h
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..96fdfc9c6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/types/wlr_linux_explicit_synchronization_v1.h
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+#ifndef TYPES_WLR_LINUX_EXPLICIT_SYNCHRONIZATION_V1_H
+#define TYPES_WLR_LINUX_EXPLICIT_SYNCHRONIZATION_V1_H
+
+#include <stdbool.h>
+#include <wayland-server-core.h>
+
+struct wlr_buffer;
+
+/**
+ * Advertises zwp_linux_explicit_synchronization_v1. Returns false when
+ * WLR_NO_EXPLICIT_SYNC is set or the global could not be created.
+ */
+bool linux_explicit_synchronization_v1_create(struct wl_display *display);
+
+/**
+ * To be called by a buffer type when its buffer is released, before it sends
+ * wl_buffer.release. Returns true when a client asked to be told through
+ * zwp_linux_buffer_release_v1 instead - it has been, and wl_buffer.release
+ * must not be sent for this cycle.
+ */
+bool linux_explicit_synchronization_v1_release_buffer(struct wlr_buffer *buffer);
+
+#endif
